\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces How server load is wired in Temoa, in every hour and every region. Public generators feed the \texttt  {electricity} commodity, which serves the regular grid load. Eligible clean generators built for servers feed a separate \texttt  {server\_electricity} commodity, which serves the regulated server load (\texttt  {DEMAND\_SERVERS\_45V}). A one-way converter (\texttt  {server\_to\_elec}) lets surplus server electricity spill into the public grid; nothing flows the other way.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:wiring}{{1}{2}{How server load is wired in Temoa, in every hour and every region. Public generators feed the \texttt {electricity} commodity, which serves the regular grid load. Eligible clean generators built for servers feed a separate \texttt {server\_electricity} commodity, which serves the regulated server load (\texttt {DEMAND\_SERVERS\_45V}). A one-way converter (\texttt {server\_to\_elec}) lets surplus server electricity spill into the public grid; nothing flows the other way}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces New-Build 3P national standing capacity in 2040 (GW) by technology family, from the pre-2027 fleet through the coverage sweep. Solid bars are public build; hatched bars are capacity built for servers. Green squares mark total battery capacity (not stacked); hollow squares mark the battery capacity built for servers. ``p1p3'' is 100\% coverage with hourly matching relaxed to annual matching.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:capacity}{{2}{3}{New-Build 3P national standing capacity in 2040 (GW) by technology family, from the pre-2027 fleet through the coverage sweep. Solid bars are public build; hatched bars are capacity built for servers. Green squares mark total battery capacity (not stacked); hollow squares mark the battery capacity built for servers. ``p1p3'' is 100\% coverage with hourly matching relaxed to annual matching}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces New-Build 3P national generation in 2040 (TWh) by technology family. Hatched segments are generation by server technologies. The purple bar beside each stack is server electricity spilled to the public grid; it is already counted in the stack and is drawn separately so it is not double-counted. Green squares mark battery discharge (not stacked). The p1p3 run has no equivalent spillover mechanism.}}{3}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:generation}{{3}{3}{New-Build 3P national generation in 2040 (TWh) by technology family. Hatched segments are generation by server technologies. The purple bar beside each stack is server electricity spilled to the public grid; it is already counted in the stack and is drawn separately so it is not double-counted. Green squares mark battery discharge (not stacked). The p1p3 run has no equivalent spillover mechanism}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces New-Build 3P, by zone: the coverage needed to mitigate server impacts on the public grid, i.e.\ the lowest tested coverage (10--100\%) at which the public grid is at or below the no-servers case for 2040 CO$_2$ (green), the 2040 demand-weighted marginal cost (dual of the demand balance, divided by the 2040 period weight; blue), and the 2027--2040 average present cost of energy (yellow). A bar labelled $\leq 10$ means the threshold was met at the lowest tested coverage. Hatched full-height bars with a cross mark impacts not mitigated by 100\% coverage; the number is how far above. The average cost includes the myopic capital-cost truncation correction.}}{4}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:geofacet}{{4}{4}{New-Build 3P, by zone: the coverage needed to mitigate server impacts on the public grid, i.e.\ the lowest tested coverage (10--100\%) at which the public grid is at or below the no-servers case for 2040 CO$_2$ (green), the 2040 demand-weighted marginal cost (dual of the demand balance, divided by the 2040 period weight; blue), and the 2027--2040 average present cost of energy (yellow). A bar labelled $\leq 10$ means the threshold was met at the lowest tested coverage. Hatched full-height bars with a cross mark impacts not mitigated by 100\% coverage; the number is how far above. The average cost includes the myopic capital-cost truncation correction}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Top: New-Build 3P present-value system cost to 2040 (\$ trillion). Each point is labelled with the flat \$/MWh rate that, charged to data centers on their whole consumption, would recover all cost above the no-servers case. Bottom: 2040 national CO$_2$ relative to the no-servers case (Mt/yr). The gas CT and gas CC points meet 100\% coverage with new gas plants instead of clean generation (no geothermal).}}{5}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:npvcost}{{5}{5}{Top: New-Build 3P present-value system cost to 2040 (\$ trillion). Each point is labelled with the flat \$/MWh rate that, charged to data centers on their whole consumption, would recover all cost above the no-servers case. Bottom: 2040 national CO$_2$ relative to the no-servers case (Mt/yr). The gas CT and gas CC points meet 100\% coverage with new gas plants instead of clean generation (no geothermal)}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces New-Build 3P at 100\% coverage: change in the public-grid average present cost of energy (2027--2040, \$/MWh, present value to 2027) relative to the no-servers case. ``Pub'' is that change; ``Srv'' is the server-side average present cost. A check mark means at or below the no-servers case; a cross means still above. NYUP ($-55.2$) is beyond the colour scale; NYCW is excluded.}}{6}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:avgcostmap}{{6}{6}{New-Build 3P at 100\% coverage: change in the public-grid average present cost of energy (2027--2040, \$/MWh, present value to 2027) relative to the no-servers case. ``Pub'' is that change; ``Srv'' is the server-side average present cost. A check mark means at or below the no-servers case; a cross means still above. NYUP ($-55.2$) is beyond the colour scale; NYCW is excluded}{figure.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces National public-side and server-side present-value average cost (\$/MWh) for the no-servers case, servers without regulation, New-Build 3P at 20--100\% coverage, and servers served by new gas CC or gas CT. The server-side cost is blended: covered MWh at the carve-out cost plus uncovered MWh at that scenario's public rate, divided by total server MWh. Server fuel in the gas cases is charged to the server side.}}{6}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:avgcostsummary}{{7}{6}{National public-side and server-side present-value average cost (\$/MWh) for the no-servers case, servers without regulation, New-Build 3P at 20--100\% coverage, and servers served by new gas CC or gas CT. The server-side cost is blended: covered MWh at the carve-out cost plus uncovered MWh at that scenario's public rate, divided by total server MWh. Server fuel in the gas cases is charged to the server side}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Hourly dispatch in TREW, a server-heavy zone where servers are about 37\% of load, for representative week 8 of 2030. Left: servers with no regulation. Right: New-Build 3P at 100\% coverage. Stacked areas are solar and wind (public and server combined); lines show load, public grid generation excluding storage, imports, and spillover from the carve-out to the public grid.}}{7}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:trewhourly}{{8}{7}{Hourly dispatch in TREW, a server-heavy zone where servers are about 37\% of load, for representative week 8 of 2030. Left: servers with no regulation. Right: New-Build 3P at 100\% coverage. Stacked areas are solar and wind (public and server combined); lines show load, public grid generation excluding storage, imports, and spillover from the carve-out to the public grid}{figure.8}{}}
